# ============================================================================
# Local environment configuration
# ============================================================================
# This file is COMMITTED, deliberately, and ships empty.
#
# `.env` is declared under `flutter: assets:` in pubspec.yaml. A declared asset
# that does not exist fails the build during asset bundling, before any Dart
# runs — so a fresh clone could not build at all while this file was gitignored.
# Committing it empty is what makes `git clone && flutter build` work.
#
# It contains no keys on purpose. Every lookup falls through to the defaults in
# AppConfig, so this file changes nothing until you put something in it.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# To configure your local machine
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy the settings you need out of `.env.example` and fill them in below. At
# minimum the app needs:
#
#   SUPABASE_URL=https://<your-project-id>.supabase.co
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon-key>
#
# Then tell git to stop tracking your edits, so your keys can never be
# committed by an absent-minded `git add -A`:
#
#   git update-index --skip-worktree .env
#
# To undo that later (e.g. to pull an update to this file):
#
#   git update-index --no-skip-worktree .env
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WARNING
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything in this file is bundled into the app and served at a public URL on
# web builds. Never put SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY here — it bypasses every RLS
# policy. See docs/audit/2026-08-04-code-audit.md (F4).
# ============================================================================
